  "summary": "Interpreting contrastive learning as representation learning with paired positive and negative examples, only four supplied candidates directly apply that method to mapping active wildfire extent. [V0189] reports the strongest higher-is-better exact-match score on FireScope (AUROC 0.94). [V0191] evaluates the same method-topic pairing on MetroFlow with accuracy 0.73, [V0190] on ChurnBench with test F1 0.66, and [V0192] on Atlas-ICU with MAE 0.80; MAE is an error metric where lower is better, so these results are not like-for-like comparable across datasets and metrics. No fifth supplied candidate meets both criteria; [V0173] is included only to satisfy the required five-ID output as a same-topic FireScope comparator, but it uses self-attention encoder models (AUROC 0.85), not contrastive learning.",
